# This package is consumed by nine sibling frontend images (the warehouse-console
# shell and the eight bounded-context Module Federation remotes), each of which
# supplies this checkout to Docker as a named build context:
#
#   docker build --build-context uikit=../../warehouse-ui-kit .
#
# Without this file, the developer's local node_modules is copied into those
# Linux builders. That tree only ever contains the host platform's binaries for
# the native dependencies Vite 8 pulls in (@rolldown/binding-darwin-arm64,
# lightningcss-darwin-*, @oxlint/binding-darwin-*), so npm inside the image
# treats those packages as already installed, never fetches the linux ones, and
# the build dies with:
#
#   Error: Cannot find native binding ... Cannot find module
#   '@rolldown/binding-linux-arm64-gnu'
#
# (npm/cli#4828). Excluding node_modules forces every image to resolve its own
# platform's binaries, and incidentally drops ~176MB from the build context.
node_modules
dist

# Local build/test noise that never affects the published bundle.
.vite
coverage
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store

.git
.gitignore
.github
docs
README.md
